&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Fanatics Commerce is the global leader in licensed sports merchandise, operating a vertically integrated platform that designs, manufactures, and delivers officially licensed apparel, jerseys, headwear, and collectibles for major leagues, teams, and events worldwide. With more than 900 e-commerce sites and a global omnichannel presence across digital, in-venue, and retail, Fanatics Commerce reaches fans in over 180 countries and powers official fan experiences for many of the world&#39;s most iconic sports properties.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Fanatics, we bring our BOLD Leadership Principles to life every day - building championship teams, obsessing over fans, acting with entrepreneurial speed, and delivering with a determined and relentless mindset.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Head of Operations – EU Fulfilment&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fanatics Commerce is the global leader in licensed sports merchandise, operating a vertically integrated platform that designs, manufactures, and delivers officially licensed apparel, jerseys, headwear, and collectibles for major leagues, teams, and events worldwide. With more than 900 e-commerce sites and a global omnichannel presence across digital, in-venue, and retail, Fanatics Commerce reaches fans in over 180 countries and powers official fan experiences for many of the world&#39;s most iconic sports properties.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Fanatics, we bring our BOLD Leadership Principles to life every day—building championship teams, obsessing over fans, acting with limitless entrepreneurial spirit, and delivering with a determined and relentless mindset.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As we continue to scale our global platform, the Head of Operations – EU Fulfilment will play a critical role in leading end-to-end customer fulfilment capability across the EU region.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ROLE OVERVIEW&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting to the Vice President, Operations and based in France, the Head of Operations – EU Fulfilment is responsible for leading and directing customer fulfilment across the EU region, building capacity and capability through both owned and third-party operations to service all verticals. The role owns the development and execution of operational strategies that improve speed of delivery, reduce cost, and drive down defects across the full supply chain from first to final mile. The Head of Operations – EU Fulfilment delivers business and fan impact through BOLD leadership and execution excellence, leveraging data, automation, and AI-enabled insights.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;HOW WILL YOU DRIVE IMPACT&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Success is measured by the ability to deliver results through BOLD capabilities and measurable outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Leadership:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with business leaders and stakeholders across the UK and EU, operational leaders spanning supply chain, freight, fulfilment, and final mile, and local technical and functional teams to align operational plans with broader business priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strengthen the France-based operational partnership with internal stakeholders across the international Senior Leadership Team, influencing effectively within a regional, matrixed environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;People Leadership:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and develop high-performing teams with clear ownership across key partners, verticals, and locations, fostering a culture of collaboration, transparency, and continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate operational excellence standards into 3PL environments, embedding accountability and performance ownership across all third-party operators.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fan &amp;amp; Customer Impact&lt;/strong&gt; (Obsessed with Fans)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute strategies to improve customer and partner satisfaction through faster delivery, lower cost, and reduced defect rates across the EU region.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive operational plans that support all verticals and locales, ensuring consistent service quality and fulfilment performance for fans across every channel.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage vendor performance, contracts, and service delivery to ensure all partners meet or exceed agreed service levels and customer experience standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the selection and onboarding of new providers to support the growth plans of verticals and locales within the EU region.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Innovation &amp;amp; Problem Solving&lt;/strong&gt; (Limitless Entrepreneurial Spirit)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate capital expenditure projects into tangible ROI and measurable service benefits, ensuring investment decisions are grounded in data and operational insight.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and implement plans to improve speed to delivery while simultaneously reducing cost and defects, identifying synergies across the EU region to optimise performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a change leader and owner, driving continuous improvement across 3PL and internal operations through innovative thinking and structured execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ownership &amp;amp; Execution&lt;/strong&gt; (Determined &amp;amp; Relentless Mindset)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the operations forecast and plans end-to-end, ensuring alignment between operational capacity and business demand across all EU verticals and locations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Optimise the speed and cost of service across the region, balancing efficiency with service quality and partner commitments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive operational synergies across the EU region, identifying and realising efficiencies that benefit customers, partners, and the broader Fanatics Commerce business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI &amp;amp; DIGITAL CAPABILITY&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are building a future-ready organization. This role is expected to:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply AI and technology to improve efficiency, quality, and outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use data and digital tools to inform decisions and enhance performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrate curiosity and adaptability in adopting new technologies and ways of working&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to a culture of innovation and continuous improvement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CAPABILITIES &amp;amp; EXPERIENCE YOU BRING&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of operational leadership experience within complex, multi-site or omni-channel organisations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience managing 3PLs, including SLA ownership, contract management, and performance governance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of the end-to-end supply chain, from first mile through to final mile delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated track record as a change leader, owning and driving transformation across operational environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effective communicator and influencer with the ability to operate in regional, matrixed stakeholder environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;France-based operational experience is essential, with the ability to lead on-the-ground operations from a France base.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing and executing operational plans that deliver measurable improvements in speed, cost, and quality across multiple verticals and geographies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WORK LOCATION&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hybrid: The primary place of performance of this role is the Company&#39;s office located in Paris, France, subject to the Company&#39;s current hybrid work policy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;At Fanatics, we operate with a BOLD mindset - We Build Championship Teams, we’re Obsessed with Fans, we embrace a Limitless Entrepreneurial Spirit, and we approach every challenge with a Determined and Relentless Mindset. If you’re ready to contribute to a dynamic, fast-paced environment that thrives on collaboration and growth, we want you to be part of our team.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;ABOUT US&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Fanatics is building a leading global digital sports platform. We ignite the passions of global sports fans and maximize the presence and reach for our hundreds of sports partners globally by offering products and services across Fanatics Commerce, Fanatics Collectibles, and Fanatics Betting &amp;amp; Gaming, allowing sports fans to Buy, Collect, and Bet. Through the Fanatics platform, sports fans can buy licensed fan gear, jerseys, lifestyle and streetwear products, headwear, and hardgoods; collect physical and digital trading cards, sports memorabilia, and other digital assets; and bet as the company builds its Sportsbook and iGaming platform. Fanatics has an established database of over 100 million global sports fans; a global partner network with approximately 900 sports properties, including major national and international professional sports leagues, players associations, teams, colleges, college conferences and retail partners, 2,500 athletes and celebrities, and 200 exclusive athletes; and over 2,000 retail locations, including its Lids retail stores. Our more than 22,000 employees are committed to relentlessly enhancing the fan experience and delighting sports fans globally.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;ABOUT THE TEAM&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Fanatics Commerce is a leading designer, manufacturer, and seller of licensed fan gear, jerseys, lifestyle and streetwear products, headwear, and hardgoods. It operates a vertically-integrated platform of digital and physical capabilities for leading sports leagues, teams, colleges, and associations globally – as well as its flagship site, &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.fanatics.com&quot;&gt;www.fanatics.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Fanatics Commerce has a broad range of online, sports venue, and vertical apparel partnerships worldwide, including comprehensive partnerships with leading leagues, teams, colleges, and sports organizations across the world—including the NFL, NBA, MLB, NHL, MLS, Formula 1, and Australian Football League (AFL); the Dallas Cowboys, Golden State Warriors, Paris Saint-Germain, Chelsea FC, and Tokyo Giants; the University of Notre Dame, University of Alabama, and University of Texas; the International Olympic Committee (IOC), England Rugby, and the Union of European Football Associations (UEFA).&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;At Fanatics Commerce, we infuse our BOLD Leadership Principles in everything we do:&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;· Build Championship Teams&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;· Obsessed with Fans&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;· Limitless Entrepreneurial Spirit&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;· Determined and Relentless Mindset&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;By submitting your application, you agree to our terms of service and acknowledge you have read our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://static1.squarespace.com/static/5ff494b9931735466ce28d5b/t/69de53bde2c02c25e9c38758/1776178110037/Candidate+Privacy+Policy+April+2026.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Candidate Privacy Policy.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Fanatics will never ask candidates for money, banking information, or other sensitive personal information as part of the interview process. If you receive a suspicious message claiming to be from Fanatics recruiting, please do not respond and report it &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a -----
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location: &lt;/strong&gt;Remote within Europe, with regular presence in Bremen&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Direct Reports:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;None initially&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Working Model: &lt;/strong&gt;Remote / hybrid. Regular time on-site in Bremen.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Mission&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Own the product direction for Constructor&#39;s quantum software line and act as the bridge between a research group and a technology platform. This is a hands-on role in a small technical team, not portfolio management. The Head of Product decides what gets built, keeps research and engineering pointed at something shippable, and owns the relationship with the customers and partners who use it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pillar 1 Product Direction&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the roadmap for the quantum software line and the decisions behind it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define which capabilities go into the Constructor technology platform and in what order.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate research capability into product that someone outside the group will pay for or use.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Kill work that is not going anywhere, and say so clearly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Success Metrics and KPIs: roadmap delivered, features adopted, decisions made and held.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pillar 2 Research and Engineering Interface&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sit between physicists and engineers and keep both productive.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run planning and prioritisation for a small, senior, opinionated team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hold the technical depth to challenge both sides rather than relay between them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Accountability: research output converted into shipped product.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pillar 3 External Engagement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own customer, partner and vendor relationships directly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Constructor Tech and Constructor University on joint offerings and teaching applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent the group externally at conferences and with partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Success Metrics and KPIs: partner engagements initiated and sustained, external visibility of the group.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Requirements&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical background in physics, engineering or computer science, with enough depth to hold your own with research scientists.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Taken scientific or deep-tech software from research prototype to product.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run customer and partner engagements personally, not through a sales team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Worked somewhere small enough that the product person also does the work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills &amp;amp; Competencies&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong facilitation. You will be the person keeping a room of physicists on track.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable being the only product person present.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to say no and explain why.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear communication with technical and non-technical audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Education &amp;amp; Languages&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Degree in a technical discipline; postgraduate qualification an advantage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent English.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What This Role Is (and Is Not)&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This role IS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on, senior, and accountable for what the group ships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A role with real decision authority over direction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Externally facing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This role is NOT&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A programme or portfolio management role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A role with a product team reporting into it from day one.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A commercial role without technical substance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;At Sword, we’re building AI to heal billions and unlock humanity’s full potential. In doing so, we’re pioneering AI Care, a fundamentally new approach to healthcare built for medical reasoning, safety, and real-time treatment, not generic technology applied after the fact. As both a clinical-centric frontier AI lab and an applied AI platform, Sword is reimagining how care is delivered at scale, removing traditional barriers like appointments, waiting rooms, and stigma so more people can access the care they need—and ultimately get back to lives lived in full.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Since 2020, Sword has expanded across physical therapy, women’s health, cardiometabolic, and mental health, and is now moving beyond the session to a fully AI-native, 24/7 care program that brings physical activity, therapeutic exercise, psychotherapy, nutrition, and behavior change into one connected experience. More than 700,000 members across three continents have completed over 10 million AI sessions, helping 1,000+ enterprise clients avoid more than $1 billion in unnecessary healthcare costs. Backed by 42 clinical studies, 44+ patents, and more than $500 million raised from leading investors including Khosla Ventures, General Catalyst, and Founders Fund, Sword is defining a new standard for healthcare.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;AI&amp;nbsp;Proficiency at Sword&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;AI fluency is a core expectation at Sword. Every candidate is assessed against our three-level framework — be ready to share real examples of how AI is already part of how you work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Explorer (Level 1) — Uses AI daily to boost personal productivity&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Builder (Level 2) — Creates workflows and tools that elevate the whole team&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Integrator (Level 3) — Embeds AI into products and processes at scale&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Every hire must demonstrate at least Level 1. The expected level will vary depending on the seniority of the role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;AI Care Operations (previously Sword Intelligence), is Sword&#39;s AI care management division. We don&#39;t deliver a clinical program to members. We deploy AI Care Managers, trained on more than 14 million real care interactions, to run the operations of providers, payers and national health systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It started as an internal problem. On the way to freeing over a million people from pain, Sword hit the same wall every healthcare organization does: we didn&#39;t have enough hands to scale the care we needed to provide. Instead of hiring our way out, we built AI to do it, certified it for clinical use, and ran it in our own operations before offering it to anyone else.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Today we sell two families of solutions:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Triage&lt;/strong&gt; — a certified Clinical Triage Line that guides every patient to the right care, 24/7, across voice and digital channels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Care Orchestration&lt;/strong&gt; — care navigation, population health campaigns (screenings, vaccinations, medication adherence), surgery prehab and rehab, and readmission prevention.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;ve announced a partnership with the Hellenic Ministry of Health to build an AI-powered front door for Greece&#39;s 10 million citizens, and we work with other national health systems, health plans and providers across the US and Europe. The US is now our biggest growth opportunity, and this role is central to capturing it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;The role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are hiring a Head of Go-to-Market for AI Care Operations in the US. The role sits at the intersection of product marketing, competitive intelligence and commercial enablement. It is one of the leadership roles on the AI Care Operations team, reporting to the General Manager.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Here&#39;s the opportunity. &quot;AI agents for healthcare&quot; is one of the most crowded categories in the market right now. Voice AI startups, EHR vendors, care management platforms and outsourcers all claim to automate care operations, and to a buyer they can sound alike. Very few of them have certified medical devices, national-scale partnerships, or AI proven on hundreds of thousands of their own members before it was sold to anyone else. We have all three. Your job is to make that difference unmistakable.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will own three things:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Make our value impossible to miss.&lt;/strong&gt; Build the narrative, positioning and competitive differentiation that make it obvious why AI Care Operations is categorically better than AI point solutions, legacy nurse lines and call centers, and the care management platforms buyers already have. That means the core messaging architecture across Triage and Care Orchestration, positioning by buyer (health plan, health system, value-based care, employer, government), battle cards, ROI frameworks, and the demos and proof that move a skeptical COO or VP of Care Management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Make sure the commercial team can tell that story.&lt;/strong&gt; Sword&#39;s segment sales teams sell many solutions and can&#39;t be experts in all of them. When the health plan team is in front of a Medicare Advantage plan, or the employer team is pitching a front door for a self-insured population, they come to you to scope the workflows, walk the buyer through how the agents actually work, and answer the hard questions on safety, integration and ROI.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Find, surface and pursue the opportunities.&lt;/strong&gt; You will canvass the US and international markets systematically for the accounts, RFPs, procurements, contract renewals and budget signals that would otherwise go unnoticed: a health plan rebuilding its care management operation, a health system under readmission penalties, a state agency tendering a nurse line. You&#39;ll use AI tooling to do this faster and wider than a traditional GTM team could, then partner with the relevant segment leader to make sure each opportunity is pursued and won.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;AI proficiency at Sword&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;AI fluency is a core expectation at Sword, and every candidate is assessed against our three-level framework: Explorer (uses AI daily for personal productivity), Builder (creates workflows and tools that lift the whole team) and Integrator (embeds AI into products and processes at scale). This role requires Builder at minimum. Come ready with real examples.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll be doing&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Core positioning, messaging house and narrative architecture for AI Care Operations and each of its solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The category story: why AI care management that does the work beats both headcount and AI tools that only assist the people doing it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive intelligence and battle cards across voice AI and agentic AI vendors, nurse line and call center outsourcers, and care management platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Buyer-facing materials: one-pagers, ROI and capacity calculators, demo scripts and recorded agent calls, case studies, RFP response library, sales decks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proof architecture: turning deployments into case studies and outcome metrics (contacts handled, cost per interaction, gap closure, time to care, readmissions) that a CFO will sign off on&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solution specialist team (direct reports), paired with segment sales reps across health plans, health systems, value-based care, employers and government&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sales and customer success enablement: training, playbooks, discovery guides, certification on each solution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Market opportunity mapping and systematic canvassing across US segments, with a lighter watch on international tenders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Message consistency across Sword&#39;s commercial segments and geographies, including where AI Care Operations is sold as part of the broader AI Care platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Voice of the market into product: what buyers ask for, where we lose, and what competitors are shipping&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;We&#39;d love to see&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are currently at, or recently from, a Lead, Head, Director or VP-level GTM or product marketing role where you owned the full stack: launching products, positioning, competitive differentiation, sales enablement and market strategy. You&#39;ve built things that measurably changed how deals were won.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You can sell something that isn&#39;t a product category yet. AI Care Operations is bought by operations leaders, not benefits leaders, and it competes with a budget line (headcount, outsourcing) as much as with other vendors. You know how to make the case that replacing work is different from adding a tool, and you can tell a clean story across several solutions without it sounding like a platform pitch that means nothing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You think in first principles. Faced with a new buyer, your instinct is to ask what operational problem they actually have, why our agents solve it better than more staff or another vendor, and what evidence would make a skeptical COO believe it. You don&#39;t reach for a template.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are genuinely AI-fluent, not performatively. You&#39;ve built your own workflows and loops with AI tools for market intelligence, opportunity canvassing and competitive research. You&#39;ll also be selling AI, so you need to understand how our agents work well enough to explain their limits honestly.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You write well and think clearly. Your materials are the kind a VP of Care Management reads and thinks &quot;these people have run a care operation.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are close to the field. You&#39;ve sat in on deals, heard objections live, and changed your strategy because of what buyers said rather than what you assumed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Requirements&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years in product marketing and/or GTM, with clear ownership of positioning and competitive strategy, and current or recent Lead, Head, Director or VP scope&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ownership of all three: product marketing and positioning, GTM strategy, and sales, field or revenue enablement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience selling to operational buyers (COOs, VPs of operations or care management, contact center leaders) rather than only end users or benefits teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evidence of working cross-functionally with sales and customer success, not only corporate marketing, and of building competitive intelligence from scratch rather than inheriting it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Based in the US&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Strong signal backgrounds&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;B2B healthcare software and AI companies with strong commercial engines selling to health systems and payers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Medical device and health technology companies that sell regulated, certified products into providers and payers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Automation and AI companies whose products replace operational work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has positioned an AI or automation product that replaces labor, and built ROI cases a CFO accepted&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has built competitive displacement narratives that demonstrably changed win rates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has used AI tooling to drive market canvassing and opportunity identification at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with multi-solution, multi-segment GTM, including public sector procurement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;How success is measured&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is not a quota-carrying role, but it is not a soft one. You&#39;ll be held to:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Qualified pipeline sourced from your canvassing, by segment and pillar&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive win rate, and win rate on deals where a solution specialist was involved&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bookings influenced across health plans, health systems, value-based care, employers and government&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sales cycle length from first meeting to signed pilot or contract&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enablement adoption: how many reps can pitch, demo and handle objections on each pillar without help&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This role can sit remotely and the compensation range will be adjusted to accurately reflect the country in which the candidate resides&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal&quot; style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;*The range below reflects base, variable, and equity for this role.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal&quot; style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;This is a starting point, not a ceiling — once someone joins and proves they&#39;re outlier talent, we adjust quickly to make sure their compensation matches their impact.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal&quot; style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;Job titles may span more than one career level, so actual pay depends on skills, qualifications, experience, location, and market demand, among other factors. The range reflects base salary plus any variable, bonus, or sales incentives, and our estimate of the value of private company stock options where applicable. It&#39;s subject to change, and future stock value isn&#39;t guaranteed. Sword also offers additional benefits beyond total compensation.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Total Compensation Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$145,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$330,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
