&lt;h3&gt;About Dwelly&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Dwelly is building the AI operating system for residential lettings. Its growing network of agencies provides its AI with real-world data, continuous feedback, and control over complete workflows, making exceptional service the standard for landlords and tenants. Today, Dwelly operates more than 15,000 properties and $470 million in GMV, making it one of the UK’s ten largest lettings operators. The company has raised $263 million.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We’re a fast-growing, product-focused company, backed by top-tier investors and led by a team with deep experience in real estate, technology, and operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Position Summary&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a highly talented and hands-on Senior Product Designer to help shape the experience across the full set of Dwelly products (Tenant Find, Property Management, Payments, CRM) and the internal back-office tools that power them. This role involves deeply understanding our user personas (Tenant, Landlord, Maintenance Contractor, Dwelly Agent) and designing for both the customer-facing portals and the operational tools our agents use every day.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Given the early stage of the business, our current products are hyper-functional but quite basic — an &quot;MVP&quot; that prioritises getting the job done across all domains. You&#39;ll work closely with product and engineering to take these to the next level: bringing clarity, usability, and craft to data-dense, workflow-heavy internal tools, and building genuinely good experiences for tenants and landlords. You&#39;ll also help establish the basic building blocks of design at Dwelly — a shared design system, patterns, and a lightweight design process — from the ground up.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our current development team is a team of 5, a few analysts, and one product designer. You&#39;ll join a small, fast-moving product team and have an outsized impact on how the whole product looks, feels, and works.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1. &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;User Research &amp;amp; Insights&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with product to understand user pain points across all personas — tenants, landlords, maintenance contractors, and internal agents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn qualitative and quantitative insights into design decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as an advocate for usability and the end user within the company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2. End-to-End Product Design&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design flows, wireframes, and high-fidelity UIs for both customer-facing products (tenant and landlord portals) and internal back-office tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design for data-dense, workflow-heavy operational products where clarity and efficiency matter more than decoration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the design process from concept and prototyping through to polished, build-ready specs, and iterate after launch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3. Design Across the Product Suite&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring consistency and quality across Tenant Find, Property Management, Payments, and the communications/portal layer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with engineers and product managers to translate requirements into shippable design, balancing craft with speed and technical feasibility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;4. Design System &amp;amp; Process Building&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and maintain a shared design system, component library, and reusable patterns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Introduce lightweight design workflows, documentation, and review/handoff practices suited to an early-stage team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Qualifications &amp;amp; Preferred Background:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience&amp;nbsp;in product design, with a strong portfolio spanning both complex/operational tools and consumer-facing products. Comfortable in early-stage, low-structure environments as well as more structured, product-led settings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills:&lt;/strong&gt; Strong interaction and visual design skills; systems thinking; exceptional attention to detail; able to design for complexity and make it feel simple. Excellent communication and collaboration skills across product and engineering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In step with recent technology advancements: &lt;strong&gt;can prototype and ship designs quickly and independently with the help of AI.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Background:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing operational, back-office, or B2B tools where efficiency and workflow are central — ideally in tech-enabled or operational businesses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building or contributing to a design system from scratch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong sense of ownership, a &quot;get things done&quot; attitude, and excellent attention to detail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Compensation &amp;amp; Benefits:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive salary with the potential for equity options based on performance, recognising exceptional contributions to our integration success.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What is it like being a Dwell-er?&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Feel free to check out &lt;a href=&quot;https://docsend.com/view/7v8gwrjaky7mn895&quot;&gt;Dwelly Core Principles&lt;/a&gt;. That’s about what we believe in, how we operate and make decisions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What we offer is not a fancy office or a static workplace. Instead, this is solving one of worlds’ most complex problems in the largest consumer industry in the world (residential rentals), to improve the experience for &amp;gt;30% of households (&amp;gt;5M in the UK, and &amp;gt;100M including EU and US) that live in rental homes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is about disrupting the largest, most antiquated industry in the world, with one of the strongest operational and technical teams that exist in the UK and the EU. We work hard, and we shoot for extremely ambitious results. But we want people to be proud of what they’ve built and be able to look back and say one day “hell yeah, that was me that did it all”.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Customer obsession rather than competitive focus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for invention&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operational excellence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Long-term thinking&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p data-start=&quot;556&quot; data-end=&quot;829&quot;&gt;By applying for this position, you consent to the processing and storage of your personal data for recruitment purposes for up to 365 days, in accordance with our data retention policy and applicable data protection laws.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Electra&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Air travel is about to become something more: more direct, more accessible, and more connected to the places where people live, work and want to be. Every day in the U.S., people make 35 million trips of 50–500 miles, stuck in traffic or routed through crowded hubs. Chances are, you&#39;ve been one of them. At Electra, we&#39;re changing that with the EL9, a nine-passenger, hybrid-electric aircraft that takes off and lands in just 150 feet. Our Ultra Short technology opens up thousands of new places to fly, beyond conventional runways, congested airports and long drives. We&#39;re backed by Lockheed Martin, Honeywell and Safran. Operators worldwide have signed intent-to-purchase agreements for the first 2,200 aircraft we produce, and we&#39;re moving toward first test flights in 2027.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Getting a new kind of aircraft airborne takes more than ambition. It takes our kind of bold: people who think big while working in the real world. Who move ideas into action and collaborate without silos. Who put people first and make room at the table for everyone. Who challenge one another without diminishing one another.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Sound like you? Then look beyond what you thought were your own limits, and help us take flight beyond runways.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Electra&#39;s Senior Structural Assembly Manufacturing Engineer, you&#39;ll play a key role in developing and industrializing the structural assembly processes for the EL9 aircraft, working from early product development through prototype build, production implementation, and ramp-up.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll work closely with Product Engineering during aircraft development to ensure structural designs incorporate Design for Manufacturing and Assembly (DFMA) principles and can be efficiently, repeatably, and reliably produced. You&#39;ll bring a hands-on manufacturing perspective to structural design decisions, evaluating assembly sequence, tolerance management, access, tooling, fastening and joining methods, inspection requirements, producibility, and production risk.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the EL9 transitions from design into physical hardware, you&#39;ll help translate released engineering into executable manufacturing processes and support prototype and initial aircraft builds. You&#39;ll work closely with airframe manufacturing suppliers, providing on-site Manufacturing Engineering oversight and liaison support as needed to ensure proper information flow, resolve technical and quality issues, support the incorporation of product changes and support supply chain on contract management.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is an opportunity to influence both how the aircraft is designed and how it is ultimately built, while helping establish Electra&#39;s structural assembly manufacturing supply chain capability from the ground up.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product Engineering throughout aircraft development to ensure structural designs incorporate Design for Manufacturing and Assembly (DFMA) principles and support efficient, repeatable, and scalable production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review aircraft structural designs, assemblies, drawings, models, and engineering changes from a manufacturing perspective, providing recommendations related to producibility, assembly sequence, access, tolerance stack-up, fastening and joining methods, tooling, inspection, and production risk.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in design trade studies, concept reviews, and design reviews, representing Manufacturing Engineering and identifying manufacturing constraints and opportunities early in the development cycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide Manufacturing Engineering oversight and liaison support at airframe and structural suppliers, working directly with supplier manufacturing teams to clarify design and manufacturing intent, resolve producibility and assembly issues, and maintain program execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with the airframe supplier Tooling Engineering to define assembly tooling concepts, requirements, locating strategies, interfaces, and implementation plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review supplier manufacturing approaches, build plans, assembly processes, tooling concepts, and production readiness to ensure alignment with Electra&#39;s engineering requirements and program objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support prototype fabrication, development aircraft assembly, first builds, and production implementation, providing hands-on Manufacturing Engineering support to resolve issues encountered during structural assembly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate technical resolution of manufacturing issues and nonconformances with Product Engineering, Stress, Quality, Supplier Quality, Supply Chain, and other stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Capture manufacturing lessons learned and supplier feedback from prototype and initial production builds and drive those learnings back into product design, manufacturing processes, tooling, and planning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support structural assembly production ramp-up by identifying constraints, resolving manufacturing issues, improving assembly processes, and driving improvements in quality, cost, schedule, and production rate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to the development and continuous improvement of Electra manufacturing engineering standards, methods, processes, and best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Mechanical, Aerospace, Aeronautical, Manufacturing Engineering, or a related engineering field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of aerospace manufacturing engineering experience, with significant experience in aircraft structural assembly and industrialization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong hands-on knowledge of aircraft structural assembly processes, including metallic and/or composite airframe structures, drilling, fastening, joining, shimming, sealing, alignment, and major structural integration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience applying Design for Manufacturing and Assembly (DFMA) principles during aircraft product development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience reviewing engineering drawings, 3D models, GD&amp;amp;T, tolerances, and engineering changes from a manufacturing and assembly perspective.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing manufacturing plans, assembly sequences, work instructions, tooling requirements, and manufacturing engineering documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting prototype, development, or first-production aircraft builds.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working directly with aircraft structures suppliers or manufacturing partners and supporting production activities in a factory environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to work effectively across Product Engineering, Stress, Quality, Supplier Quality, Supply Chain, Tooling, and Production organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong problem-solving skills and ability to make sound engineering recommendations in a fast-moving aircraft development environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to work effectively across internal teams and external suppliers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability and willingness to travel to supplier and manufacturing locations as required by program needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Points&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with clean-sheet aircraft development and transition from prototype into production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with major structural assemblies such as fuselage, wing, empennage, control surfaces, or other primary airframe structures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with aircraft assembly tooling, jigs, fixtures, determinant assembly, or advanced assembly methodologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with digital manufacturing tools, PLM/MES environments, manufacturing BOMs, and 3D model-based manufacturing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with supplier industrialization, production readiness assessments, or manufacturing capability reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with MRB, root cause corrective action, and production nonconformance resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with AS9100 aerospace quality management systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;This range reflects the anticipated hiring range across all eligible locations; actual compensation is determined based on your relevant experience, skills, and geographic location. Total compensation includes performance bonus and comprehensive benefits.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Compensation Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$130,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$155,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Medical, dental, and vision insurance; STD, LTD, and life insurance&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Generous PTO, sick leave, and company holidays&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Paid winter break&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;401(k) with immediate vesting&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Free catered lunches, coffee, snacks, and drinks at our Manassas headquarters&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Free on-site parking&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Electra is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. This position may be subject to ITAR requirements.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;h2&gt;About Nscale&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nscale is the GPU cloud engineered for AI. We provide cost-effective, high-performance infrastructure for AI start-ups and large enterprise customers. Nscale enables AI-focused companies to achieve superior results by reducing the complexity of AI development. Our GPU cloud bolsters technical capabilities and directly supports strategic business outcomes, including cost management, rapid innovation, and environmental responsibility.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We thrive on a culture of relentless innovation, ownership, and accountability, where every team member takes pride in their work and drives it with excellence and urgency. As an Nscaler, you’ll build trust through openness and transparency, where everyone is inspired to do their best work. If you join our team, you’ll be contributing to building the technology that powers the future.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About the Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re hiring an &lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;textBold&quot;&gt;Infrastructure Engineer (OpenStack Ironic Specialist)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; to design, operate, and continuously improve the bare metal provisioning platforms that underpin Nscale’s infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role sits within the &lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;textBold&quot;&gt;Infrastructure Engineering team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;, which is responsible for the design, implementation, operation, and ongoing improvement of the infrastructure stack supporting both internal and customer-facing services. You’ll work closely with &lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;textBold&quot;&gt;network, compute, data centre, support, and pre-sales teams&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;, while also serving as a specialist escalation point for advanced provisioning and hardware issues.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a high-impact role focused on &lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;textBold&quot;&gt;OpenStack Ironic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;, automated hardware lifecycle management, and the reliable operation of large-scale physical infrastructure. You’ll also help connect Nscale to the broader &lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;textBold&quot;&gt;upstream OpenStack community&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;, ensuring our bare metal platforms evolve in line with real operational needs and industry direction.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll be doing&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;textBold&quot;&gt;Bare Metal Provisioning &amp;amp; Lifecycle Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;textBold&quot;&gt;Design&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; scalable and resilient bare metal provisioning platforms with a strong focus on &lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;textBold&quot;&gt;OpenStack Ironic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;2&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;textBold&quot;&gt;Own&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; the full lifecycle of physical infrastructure, including discovery, enrolment, provisioning, cleaning, deprovisioning, and hardware state management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;3&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;textBold&quot;&gt;Build&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; and maintain provisioning workflows for a wide range of hardware profiles, including &lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;textBold&quot;&gt;GPU-enabled&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; and high-performance server platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;4&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;textBold&quot;&gt;Support&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; platform upgrades, lifecycle management, and operational improvements across &lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;textBold&quot;&gt;Ironic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; and its dependencies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;textBold&quot;&gt;Automation &amp;amp; Platform Integration&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;textBold&quot;&gt;Manage&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; and improve integrations between &lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;textBold&quot;&gt;Ironic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; and related OpenStack services such as &lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;textBold&quot;&gt;Nova, Neutron, Glance, Keystone, and Placement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;2&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;textBold&quot;&gt;Drive&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; automation for hardware onboarding, firmware and BIOS configuration, deployment workflows, validation, and recovery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;3&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;textBold&quot;&gt;Implement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; infrastructure automation using &lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;textBold&quot;&gt;infrastructure-as-code&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; and configuration management approaches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;4&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;textBold&quot;&gt;Ensure&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; provisioning platforms and operational processes align with security, compliance, and operational standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;textBold&quot;&gt;Troubleshooting, Reliability &amp;amp; Operational Support&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;textBold&quot;&gt;Troubleshoot&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; complex issues across provisioning pipelines, &lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;textBold&quot;&gt;PXE/iPXE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;, BMC interfaces, out-of-band management, image deployment, network boot, and hardware compatibility.&lt;/li&gt;
